From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:35:04 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] ui-egui: a minimal interface-language mechanism (English-key TSV catalogs from the overlay)

deckcraft has no interface languages, so this adds the smallest mechanism: i18n.rs (new) holds a
registry of English plus uz-latn and uz-cyrl, each present only when the overlay supplies its
catalog (build_office.rs embeds catalog-uz-latn.tsv and catalog-uz-cyrl.tsv written by
`cargo xt i18n export`; cfg(office_uz)). The catalog format is WordCraft's (English-key TSV,
placeholder and ellipsis checks, bad lines skipped and logged). t() looks a string up in the
current language (thread-local, set from the `language` setting at the start of every frame)
and passes the result through rebrand(). UiState.language ("auto" by default, so an older
ui.json still loads), the app.language.set command (accepts uz as uz-latn) and a language picker
on the File > Account page. office_overlay.rs reads the current language for the app name. The
picker name carries the export's draft marker while Uzbek rows are unreviewed. Nothing in the
UI is translated yet: 0111 routes the P1 strings through t().
